  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-06-03T01:49:59.079Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I had recently run into the issue of controller drifting with my Oculus Rift S, specifically the left joystick. I’m not the first to experience such an issue, so I am proposing the idea of reassign the movement with the joysticks. This could be done by adding an additional toggle in the bindings menu which would assign the general locomotion to the right controller and turning to the left controller. This  could also be seen as an accessibility feature for our left handed users or those who would generally find the inverted controls to be more comfortable to use. I thank you for reading this and ask that you may consider this idea for a future update if you haven’t already.",
